# L §5.19 observations, L §3.1 holes: a row's field may be a hole, `paid_from: ?"whose money paid?"`, and "a read of a
# hole is that hole" (L §3.1; HOLE-INPUT shape, L §8.1, naming the row).  q1: the attribute itself; q2: compared with a
# key, an order or a guard reads it so (`==` over a hole is a hole, L §3.1); q3: the known row's attribute stays known.
# (refcore 2.0 kept the row's hole marker raw: q1 printed it and q2 was refused LOAD-UNIT "ania and ('hole', ...)
# compared", a 2.0 interpreter fault found by the probe writer's p20, writer 11.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-02-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31

source s "s"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

kind persons: parties
kind withdrawals: transfers
  attr paid_from: key persons

place sav: accounts DUK lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input bank_rows: observed

version cast
  cite s
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1988-04-12..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1986-09-03..

version rows
  cite s
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-03
  opening[sav] = 1000.00 DUK at 2026-01-01 start "line 0"
  bank_rows[r1] = (on: 2026-01-25, kind: withdrawals, leg cash from sav to world amount 900.00 DUK, paid_from: ?"whose money paid?") "line 1"
  bank_rows[r2] = (on: 2026-01-26, kind: withdrawals, leg cash from sav to world amount 50.00 DUK, paid_from: tomek) "line 2"

ask q1: o.paid_from for o in withdrawals over 2026-01-25..2026-01-25
ask q2: o.paid_from == ania for o in withdrawals over 2026-01-25..2026-01-25
ask q3: o.paid_from for o in withdrawals over 2026-01-26..2026-01-26
=== expect
q1 (o = bank_rows[r1]): ?"whose money paid?" (bank_rows[r1])
...
q2 (o = bank_rows[r1]): ?"whose money paid?" (bank_rows[r1])
...
q3 (o = bank_rows[r2]): tomek
...
